"pull" fetches the pull-request heads of each GitHub remote, but only those that are relevant to
the clone.  Pull request 1's head is a commit that the clone has and that is on no remote branch.
Pull request 2's head is a commit that the clone lacks, so it is not fetched.  Pull request 3's
head is a commit that the clone lacks, but an earlier pull fetched an earlier head of pull request
3.  The remote no longer has pull request 4, so its ref is deleted.  Pull request 5's head is in
the main branch, so it is not fetched.  Remote "other" has pull request 6, and is not on GitHub.
Remote "gone" no longer exists, so the ref of its pull request 7 is deleted.
